BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Roller Disco Daze
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260724T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260724T220000
UID:260716DjWj5Box80ahw1wBZQt7Rw
DESCRIPTION:Marin Center presents Roller Disco Daze\, a free community rol
 ler skating experience on Lagoon Island at the Marin County Fairgrounds. R
 unning Wednesdays through Sundays\, July 17 through August 16\, the rink i
 s open to all ages and skill levels\, with themed nights every Friday\, Sa
 turday\, and Sunday to keep things lively all summer long. \n\nSkate bene
 ath a disco ball surrounded by the lagoon\, then cool down with lawn games
 \, explore art installations by local artists on display\, and don't miss 
 the giant inflatable skate for the ultimate photo opp. A DJ spins on-site 
 beginning at 12 pm every Friday-Sunday to keep the music on point and the 
 vibes rolling. Food from Manny's Tacos will be on-site all days of the eve
 nt\, and Lobo's Ice Cream will be available July 17-19 and July 24-26.\n\n
 Admission is free. Skate rentals\, including kids' sizes\, are available o
 n-site for $5. All skaters must sign a waiver\; skaters under 18 require a
  parent or guardian signature.
LOCATION:Lagoon Island\, Marin County Fairgrounds
URL:https://marincenter.marincounty.gov/node/306
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Music Friday: The Northern Still
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260724T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260724T200000
UID:260715ox9PrMTmkEOzI_kqKdl6XA
DESCRIPTION:Dawn Angelosante’s \\(piano\\) voice wraps lyrics into a dre
 amscape of sound and story\, touching on love\, friendship\, heartbreak\, 
 and self-reflection. Tony Gibson’s \\(guitar\\) songwriting blends infec
 tious melodies with honest\, emotionally resonant lyrics. His music feels 
 familiar and fresh.  Michael Fecskes \\(cello\\)\, a classically trained 
 cellist and composer\, adds a unique depth to the group’s sound.  His c
 ompositions are rich and soulful.\n\nTogether\, they form The Northern Sti
 ll\, a dynamic acoustic/folk-pop trio. Since 2021 they’ve combined their
  individual voices and musical influences into a lush\, intimate sound\, w
 ith haunting vocal harmonies. Whether performing original compositions or 
 their fresh takes on covers\, they’ve captivated audiences throughout th
 e North Bay.
LOCATION:Coal Shed Brewery
URL:https://www.mareislandbrewingco.com/events/live-music-friday-07242026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jayne-Russell
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260724T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260724T193000
UID:2607146-icnse8tUC77G0znmJUGQ
DESCRIPTION:$25 General Admission Doors at 7:30pm.\n\nShow from 8:15-10:30
 pm with one intermission\n\nEarlybirds!\n\n$5 off each ticket when you use
  the code earlybird3 at checkout.\n\nOffer ends July 19th.\n\nPromo Codes
  are not applicable at the door.\n\nCodes are not case sensitive\, but m
 ust be typed as one word.\n\nSinger-songwriter-guitarist Doug Jayne is c
 o-owner of The Next Record Store in Santa Rosa\, CA\, and hosts Midday Mus
 ic on Sonoma County's NPR affiliate\,KRCB FM. Founder of Jackalope Records
 \, an indie label and recording studio\, Doug has produced dozens of North
 ern California bands and musicians since 1996. Over the years\, Doug has f
 ronted the mildly popular bands\, Stupid White People\, Loser Friendly\, L
 aughing Gravy\, and ClusterFolk.  Doug currently plays with his long-time
  collaborator\, Kevin Russell\, as Jayne-Russell\, doing mostly his origin
 al songs\, and some cool covers.\n\nhttps://www.reverbnation.com/dougjayne
  \n\nKevin Russell is a multi-instrumentalist\, singer and songwriter. H
 e performs regularly in a number of Sonoma county’s most popular bands. 
 All of these groups perform at local club venues\, county fairs\, parties\
 , festivals\, weddings and special events. For nine years Kevin was the dr
 iving force behind The Sebastopol Guitar Festival and currently is the org
 anizer of the Sonoma County Americana Music Festival held in early October
 . In addition to being a musician\, Kevin hosts shows featuring touring mu
 sicians like Joe Craven\, Gonzalo Bergara\, Jim Hurst\, David Lindley\, Ra
 dney Foster\, Jack Tempchin\, Ray Bierl\, Mike Dowling\, Laurie Lewis\, Ka
 thy Kallick\, Missy Raines\, Maria Muldaur & others.\n\nSee thefamiliarst
 rangersmusic.com for more info.
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FHu0
 0000yivezMAA
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
