BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vallejo Shakespeare in the Park- Richard III
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T190000
UID:260714npcbAq0JMUm2uaJxpcAhfA
DESCRIPTION:No chairs provided – Bring a blanket or low chair to sit on.
 \n\n"Now is the winter of our discontent\, made glorious summer by this su
 n of York"\n\nThe dust has yet to settle on the final battle of the War of
  the Roses\, a bitter conflict between the houses of York and Lancaster. H
 enry VI\, the former king\, is deposed and slain. His wife\, Margaret\, ba
 nished. Seated on the throne is Edward Plantagenet IV\, and a period of pe
 ace has graced fair England. But in the background\, treasonous plots stir
 . Richard\, newly appointed Duke of Gloucester and brother to the king\, p
 uts into motion a plan to place himself on the throne. Through manipulatio
 n\, murder\, and conspiracy\, he claws his way to the heights of England's
  power. But can one hold the loyalty of an entire kingdom through such tac
 tics? Or will fate curse the very man who thought himself above all others
 ?\n\nDirected by Nez Gray-Freeman\n\nAll shows in the park at 4 p.m.\n\nJu
 ly 25 & 21 Hanns Park\, Vallejo\n\nAugust 1 Marina Pavilion Green\, Benici
 a\n\nAugust 2 Susana Park\, Martinez\n\nAugust 8 Independence Park\, Ameri
 can Canyon\n\nAugust 9 Lower Dracena Park\, Piedmont\n\nFinal fundraiser s
 hows August 14 & 15 at 7 p.m. Vino Godfather Winery\, Vallejo $25
URL:https://www.vallejoshakespeare.org/current-show-1
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Miso & Koji: A Japanese Fermentation Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T123000
UID:260714dF0t0ces40CwrnIxA0cCjA
DESCRIPTION:Discover the magic of traditional Japanese fermentation in thi
 s hands-on workshop with chef and teacher Hiroko Kurosaki. Together we’l
 l explore the art of miso and koji\, two foundational elements of Japanese
  cuisine that bring depth\, flavor\, and nourishment to everyday meals.\n\
 nIn this class\, you will:\n\n• Make your own fresh miso to ferment at 
 home\n\n• Create two jars of seasonal vegetable ferments with salt koji\
 n\n• Taste the sweetness of traditional amazake\n\n• Leave with the kn
 owledge and confidence to continue your fermenting practice at home\n\nLea
 rn time-honored fermentation techniques and bring a piece of Japanese food
  tradition into your own kitchen.
LOCATION:Gather Sebastopol
URL:https://gathersebastopol.com/products/miso-koji-a-japanese-fermentatio
 n-workshop
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Secret Song Club presents: El Tee\, Justice Ramos-Martin\, Frances
 ca Lee
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T193000
UID:260714ZQlqp3oABEmHCr1eQCCUGQ
DESCRIPTION:$15 General Admission\n\nDoors at 7:30pm.\n\nShow from 8:15-10
 :30pm with one intermission\n\nEarlybirds!\n\n$3 off each ticket when you 
 use the code earlybird3 at checkout. Offer ends July 19th.\n\nPromo Co
 des are not applicable at the door.\n\nCodes are not case sensitive\, bu
 t must be typed as one word.\n\nCalifornian-Melbournian artist El Tee ha
 s been building a devoted following in the indie scene since 2018. The ind
 ie-folk\, alt-rock artist writes songs about grief and love and loss\, jux
 taposing her dark-mood lyrics with unassuming softness and much welcomed i
 ntimacy. In 2025\, El Tee released her EP\, ‘Kind Safe Cool’\, accompa
 nied by her second Australian national headline tour\, solidifying her rep
 utation as a compelling live performer.\n\nEl Tee released her debut album
 \, 'Everything Is Fine'\, in 2020 to critical acclaim\, earning her a shor
 tlist nod for Best Rock Act at the Music Victoria Awards and a sold-out al
 bum launch. Her music has topped Australian community radio charts\, garne
 red spins on triple J and US college radio\, and landed rotation on KEXP. 
 With a growing international presence and a new body of work in progress\,
  El Tee is poised to bring her intimate\, emotionally resonant sound to gl
 obal audiences.\n\nEl Tee has been compared to the likes of Angel Olsen an
 d Sharon Van Etten. Often backed by a four-piece band\, she has taken her 
 songs across Australia\, California\, and Europe\, sharing line-ups and fe
 stival stages with acts such as Julia Jacklin \\(US\\)\, Blake Scott \\(Au
 s\\)\, Good Morning \\(Aus\\)\, and Ryan Downey \\(Aus\\)\, steadily gathe
 ring a devoted following along the way\n\n@elteemusic Spotify: El Tee\n\nJ
 ustice Ramos-Martin is a Mexican-American singer-songwriter built on the 
  mountains and oceans of Northern California\, the stormy hills of Arkans
 as\, and the highways in between. Tastefully indoctrinated since birth by 
 a family vinyl collection\, he’s invented a sense of self and artistry t
 hrough unique guitar playing\, and honest lyrics. He writes with a pen on 
 paper\, for a human experience. Both for the listener\, and himself. His i
 nfluences include Paul Simon\, Joni Mitchell\, Jeff Buckley\, Elliot Smith
 \, The Sundays\, Gregory Alan Isakov\, and many more. In October 2025\, he
  released his debut EP Born Into a Fortune.\n\n@justiceramosmartin Spotify
 : Justice Ramos Martin\n\nFrancesca Lee is an SF-based singer-songwriter 
 whose music blends intimate storytelling\, warm expressive vocals\, and ti
 meless melodies. Her songs explore love\, memory\, and everyday detail wit
 h quiet emotional depth\, creating a grounded and personal sound rooted in
  observation and feeling\, and a distinctive voice in the contemporary sin
 ger-songwriter tradition.\n\nfrancesceleemusic.com @francescaleemusic Spot
 ify: Francesca Lee\n\nSecret Song Club is an event production organization
  that presents music parties\, songwriter showcases\, and open mics in bac
 kyards\, wineries\, and alternative venues around Sonoma County. We’re a
 ll about supporting emerging artists and creating listening spaces where p
 eople can hear music with less background chatter. Learn more at InsideLa
 nds.org https://www.instagram.com/secretsongclub
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh0
 0000AAsMLMA1
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Talks - From Mayberry to Beverly Healdsburg
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T113000
UID:260714Vz9VsDZgbU--WoqCZp5zVA
DESCRIPTION:**RUDAT Report & Downtown Before and After**\n\nJerry Haag and
  Joanne Taeuffer\n\nJust 50 years ago\, Healdsburg was seen as a cow town\
 , but an urban planning process in 1982 started the change that led to tod
 ay’s upscale version of the town. Jerry Haag\, a retired city planner\, 
 will review the process that was guided by the Regional/Urban Design Assis
 tance Team (RUDAT) leading Healdsburg to becoming a premier destination fo
 r wine country tourism.\n\nJoanne Taeuffer will show how this new vision c
 hanged the look and feel of the Plaza area from her 1960s “Mayberry” v
 ersion to what she calls “Beverly Healdsburg.”
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
