BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Watercolor Meditation Workshop with Lisa Solomon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T133000
UID:260425w7zrQHIyG0ScXAHzIBXWhw
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by the bold colors and rich patterning of the sculptu
 res featured in our Spirit Guides exhibition\, join us at Sonoma Botanical
  Garden for a hands-on watercolor workshop with Bay Area artist and maker 
 Lisa Solomon. This workshop is open to all experience levels\, from comple
 te beginners to those with prior artistic experience. In this immersive wo
 rkshop\, we’ll open up the world of color\, using painting as a means of
  exploration—and\, potentially\, relaxation. The session will begin with
  a brief\, accessible exercise to help participants become familiar with t
 he paints in their palette and comfortable working with watercolor brushes
 . From there\, Lisa will guide participants through her personal and intui
 tive approach to creating color wheels. Unlike the scientific color wheels
  many of us have encountered \\(and perhaps groaned over\\)\, this method 
 is highly individual—resulting in a wheel that is unique to each partici
 pant. This process invites reflection on how materials\, context\, and per
 sonal experience influence our perception of color\, and helps participant
 s begin to develop a deeper\, more personal relationship with it. Along th
 e way\, we’ll touch on basic color “truths\,” explore how color affe
 cts us emotionally and physically\, and discuss foundational color theory 
 and schemes. The workshop will conclude with a Color Meditation—a practi
 ce Lisa has developed and used in her own studio for years. This gentle\, 
 low-stakes exercise encourages play while fostering calm\, beauty\, and re
 laxation within an artistic practice.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabotanicalgarden.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/li
 st/watercolor-meditation-workshop-1030-am-130-pm
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
