BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tuesdays in the Plaza: Playing the Dead (Grateful Dead Tribute)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260728T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260728T200000
UID:26060508NlfdFYb0SetDqAJ3p4Pw
DESCRIPTION:Our weekly summer concerts in the Healdsburg Plaza from 6:00 p
 .m. to 8:00 p.m. provide an eclectic and unique line-up of bands\, and hav
 e been assembled to please a wide array of musical interests. Food vendors
  will be on-hand to offer locally sourced food for sale starting at 5:00 p
 .m. with the music beginning at 6:00 p.m.\n\nAbout the band: Rooted in the
  heart of San Francisco’s storied musical landscape\, Playing the Dead i
 s more than just a tribute band—they are a living\, breathing homage to 
 the spirit of the Grateful Dead and jerry garcia. Fusing improvisation\, p
 sychedelic textures\, and heartfelt musicianship\, the band captures the e
 ssence of The Dead's legendary live shows while adding their own unique sp
 ark to every performance.\n\nFormed by a collective of Bay Area musicians 
 with deep reverence for The Dead’s catalog and countercultural ethos\, P
 laying The Dead has quickly gained a loyal following throughout Northern C
 alifornia. Their shows are journeys—equal parts celebration and ceremony
 —where long-time Deadheads and new listeners alike gather to dance\, con
 nect\, and relive the magic.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza
URL:https://healdsburg.gov/335/Tuesdays-in-the-Plaza
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Teen & Young Adult Group
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260728T161500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260728T173000
UID:260603wJv797dYpEiXqsKIwzcS8Q
DESCRIPTION:Summer can bring a mix of freedom and uncertainty—more unstr
 uctured time\, shifting routines\, and social pressures that don’t take 
 a break. Our summer groups are designed to offer a supportive space where 
 teens and young adults can stay connected\, build skills\, and feel unders
 tood during this transition.\n\nAt Juniper & Jade Psychotherapy\, we belie
 ve growth happens in connection. These groups provide a safe\, therapist-l
 ed environment where participants can explore their experiences\, strength
 en relationships\, and build confidence in themselves.
LOCATION:Juniper & Jade Psychotherapy Inc
URL:https://juniperandjadepsychotherapy.com/group-therapy
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TAKE YOUR TIME: Oil Pintings by Sharon Eisley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260728T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260728T170000
UID:260529EiHwLq-Oj0uMmrY-6n7ccQ
DESCRIPTION:“Take Your Time”\n\nChange and transformation take time. I
 n her newest oil paintings Sharon Eisley explores the time as a process. B
 e it moving through grief\, re-framing your story of self\, or birthing so
 me new creation\, each painting lures you in with beautiful application th
 en holds you in time for a closer examination of our human experience. Eis
 ley's paintings are all inspired by tarot cards and her personal journey. 
 Tarot readings will be offered at the reception by @SymbolWarehouse for an
  optional small donation.\n\nOur guest artist\, Robert Benson\, will be ch
 allenging your eyes to fill in the details with his impressionist watercol
 ors.\n\nThis June 20th reception will be the FINAL art opening for Sebasto
 pol Gallery in its home of almost 20 years! This show may last only throug
 h June 2026\, then move to our new location. Or it may be up through June 
 and July. Either way\, this will be your last chance to come celebrate our
  local\, amazing group of artists at 150 N Main St.. “Take Your Time” 
 is a reminder to our collective to take our time finding and setting up ou
 r new home for all of you. I hope you can all come celebrate all the time 
 and art we shared with you in our lovely gallery.\n\nwww.sharoneisley.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
