DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T200000
UID:260722osYoeSaTTkiM2VZyRvwqbw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a summer garden party at the Community Garden outs
 ide of Petaluma Dental Group and Allume Med Spa. This special gathering is
  designed for women in Sonoma County who are looking to make new friends\,
  build meaningful connections\, and reflect on where they've been and wher
 e they're headed. Together\, we'll celebrate our accomplishments from the 
 first half of the year while planting seeds of possibility for the months 
 ahead.\n\nLocation: 1301 Southpoint Blvd\, Petaluma\, CA 94954\n\nTime: 6:
 00 - 8:00 PM\n\nAttire: Come wearing what ever makes you feel confident an
 d comfortable. No formal “garden party” outfits required.\n\nYour tick
 et includes:\n\nA private Instagram group chat: Connect with other attende
 es before the event so you can arrive already recognizing friendly faces. 
 Everyone is encouraged to follow one another and continue building relatio
 nships long after the event ends.\n\nCommunity Introductions: We'll gather
  in a circle to introduce ourselves and learn more about everyone in atten
 dance. If you're a local business owner\, this will be your opportunity to
  share about your business with the group.\n\nGuided Reflection Stations: 
 Throughout the garden\, you'll find interactive stations featuring thought
 ful prompts designed to help you celebrate your wins\, reflect on your gro
 wth\, and clarify your goals for the rest of 2026. Each guest will receive
  a worksheet to complete and take home as a reminder of the intentions the
 y set.\n\nConnection & Conversation: Share your dreams\, ideas\, and goals
  with like-minded women who believe in supporting one another. You never k
 now what opportunities\, friendships\, or collaborations may grow from a s
 imple conversation.\n\nSeasonal Refreshments: Enjoy beautiful handcrafted 
 mocktails provided by Mexology\, along with additional beverages and light
  bites while mingling throughout the garden.
LOCATION:Allume Med Spa
URL:https://www.shecanclub.com/shop/p/bloom-and-belong
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shakespeare's "As You Like It" at Chateau St. Jean Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T184500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T184500
UID:260722cMLf5j65wkewBNiMRaoivA
DESCRIPTION:Los-Angeles based Bardfly Theatre Company returns to Chateau S
 t. Jean\, Thursday July 30th & Friday July 31st\, to perform William Shak
 espeare's beloved comedy\, "As You Like It." Their unique\, immersive prod
 uction will be performed right on the grounds before the winery's historic
  Chateau. Come watch the Bard's incomparable heroine\, Rosalind\, abandon
  court life and run off to the  Forest of Arden disguised as a man\, onl
 y to cross paths with her love interest\, Orlando.\n\nThursday July 30th &
  Friday July 31st\, 2026 - Gates open at 6pm\, Show 7pm. Come early\, grab
  a glass or a bottle of wine and bites from Shugcuterie mobile charcuter
 ie bar and enjoy the view. No outside food or drink is permitted. Chairs p
 rovided. Please note\, this performance is not appropriate for children. R
 ecommended for ages 13\\+.
LOCATION:Chateau St. Jean
URL:https://www.bardflytheatreco.com/shows.html
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:July Poetry Salon: Celebrating French Poetry & Music in Downtown S
 anta Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T190000
UID:260722RtBohLY1gU2R2_yDp7Queg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special July Poetry Salon at Barrel Proof Lounge
  as we celebrate the beauty\, romance\, and artistry of French poetry and 
 music. This free evening brings together acclaimed musicians\, local poets
 \, and lovers of literature for an intimate gathering where language\, cul
 ture\, and creativity take center stage.\n\nHosted by Timothy Williams of 
 Jaxon's Press with special guest Evelyne Whitman\, this month's salon expl
 ores the rich tradition of French poetry through live readings and authent
 ic French music.\n\nThe evening features a performance by SonoTriette\, a 
 celebrated ensemble dedicated to the timeless songs of France\, including:
 \n\nMimi Pirard – Paris-born vocalist whose expressive performances brin
 g the classic French chanson tradition to life. Jan Martinelli – Veteran
  Bay Area bassist and pianist whose versatile musicianship spans jazz\, fo
 lk\, and world music. Robert Lunceford – Accomplished accordionist and c
 o-founder of SonoMusette\, known for recreating the sound and spirit of th
 e cafés of Paris.\n\nFeatured poetry readings by:\n\nKaren FitzGerald Don
 na Emerson Karen Bramblett Pat Nolan Lance Harmening and additional featur
 ed readers.\n\nWhether you're passionate about poetry\, fascinated by Fren
 ch culture\, or simply looking for a unique evening in Downtown Santa Rosa
 \, the Poetry Salon offers a welcoming "listening room" where every word a
 nd every note is meant to be savored.\n\nEvent Details\n\n Thursday\, Jul
 y 30\, 2026  5:00–7:00 PM  Barrel Proof Lounge 501 Mendocino Ave. Down
 town Santa Rosa\, CA\n\nFREE Admission\n\nPerfect for fans of:\n\nPoetry r
 eadings Spoken word French literature French chanson Live acoustic music L
 iterary events in Sonoma County Free things to do in Downtown Santa Rosa\n
 \nCome celebrate poetry\, music\, and the enduring spirit of France with a
 n evening of exceptional performances and inspiring conversation.\n\n21+\n
 \nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for more events in Downtown Sant
 a Rosa.
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/july-poetry-salon-celebrating-french-poet
 ry-music-in-downtown-santa-rosa-tickets-1993577461854?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
