SUMMARY:Wait Wait… Don't Tell Me!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T073000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T073000
UID:260722MRFKhiQuWE6jJ63yCxaQbw
DESCRIPTION:Wait Wait… Don’t Tell Me! NPR’s Peabody Award-winning co
 medy news quiz show hosted by Peter Sagal Thursday\, July 30 at 7:30 p.m. 
 Weill Hall \\+ Lawn Wait Wait… Don’t Tell Me! is National Public Radio
 ’s Peabody Award-winning comedy news quiz show. Host Peter Sagal leads a
  rotating panel of comedians\, writers\, listener contestants\, and celebr
 ity guests through a rollicking review of the week’s news. Contestants v
 ie for the most coveted prize in all of public radio: a custom-recorded gr
 eeting by any of our cast members for their voicemail. Every week\, Wait\,
  Wait…. Don’t Tell Me! records in front of a live audience\, then care
 fully edits out all the raunchy\, inappropriate\, shocking\, and hilarious
  stuff so we can broadcast something that doesn’t get NPR in trouble… 
 well\, more trouble. The only way you can find out what our panelists and 
 guests really think about the news is to come see for yourself. And please
 —don’t tell NPR. Also\, we’re all much more attractive than we sound
 . Supported in part by Cartograph Wines. Info and tickets at https://gmc.s
 onoma.edu/wait-wait-dont-tell-me
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/988887567048769/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Joy of Astonishment - An Evening of Magic and Mentalism
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T220000
UID:260715nkDF8dWmdES13TlypBfvDg
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to experience the impossible with magician and menta
 list Robert Goleman at The California Theatre! Audiences and critics alike
  have hailed Goleman's performances as "nothing short of astonishing". In 
 an age where digital personalities dominate and viral content shapes trend
 s\, Robert Goleman has remained absent from social media for more than a d
 ecade. Offering theater goers something refreshingly different - a perform
 ance shrouded in mystery that can only be experienced in person. "Live the
 ater is about connection\, presence\, and the thrill of the unexpected\," 
 says Goleman. "Each show is a singular event\, crafted to engage and aston
 ish every audience member." As the performance unfolds\, you'll find yours
 elf captivated not only by Robert's remarkable skill\, but also by the tan
 gible connection he establishes with his guests. Every demonstration is pe
 rformed with a masterful touch that blends suspense\, humor\, and genuine 
 engagement\, making every moment feel personal. All-Ages! Doors open 6:30 
 pm. TICKETS ZONE A \\(Close to the action\\) $35 ZONE B \\(Middle of the h
 ouse\\) $28 ZONE C \\(In the back\\) $21 Tickets at Door \\(ZONE C only\\)
  $35 - So buy in advance! \\(plus $2 card processing fee\\)
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/the-joy-of-astonishment-an-evening-of
 -magic-and-mentalism/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
