BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Painting in Fauve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T180000
UID:260715UAiyLrInG0aEqZDv8_I-oA
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  7/15/26\n\n**AUGUST EXHIBIT: PAI
 NTING IN FAUVE**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **July 27 – August 30\, 2026**\n\n*
 *RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, August 1\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Willow La
 Land and Gen Zorich\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be
  sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautif
 ul work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma wi
 ne country artist\, **Willow LaLand** presents **Painting in Fauve\,** a c
 ollection of oil and acrylic paintings focusing on our region’s vibrant 
 beauty through the artist’s Fauvist lens.  Known for her hyper-realisti
 c landscapes\, these works take an imaginative turn to the fantastical\, t
 apping into the wild Fauve vivid color palette.   Highlighting the show\
 , “Mt. Tamalpais” comes alive\, swathed in rich colors cascading over 
 its undulating slopes\, while rich foreground purple/blues heighten the mo
 untain’s grandeur.  “Fitch Mountain” similarly seems to sing with c
 olor as it overlooks a lush vineyard.  LaLand’s color lens takes us fro
 m palette to palate as she captures the luxuriant purple/reds of a fine re
 d wine in “Sommelier’s Dream.”  Reflecting on her creative process\
 , LaLand notes “I love the artistic freedom to play\, create depth in co
 lor\, and give a tangible realistic impression within a completely fantast
 ical expression.”\n\nA third-generation artist\, LaLand started her stud
 ies as a young girl and had a studio space at 10 years old.  She is inspi
 red by early American realists and uses traditional techniques to achieve 
 dramatic realism.  LaLand finds the Fauve color palette elicits a joyful 
 response to her themes of nature and wine.  Many of her collectors love b
 oth her styles and have a hard time\, though they vastly differ\, choosing
  between the two.  LaLand exhibits widely\, including internationally\, a
 nd participated in the Art Trails Program.  She was featured in American 
 Art Collector magazine in 2013 and on KRCB in 2015.\n\nMeet the artist: La
 Land will host the Gallery on August 2\, 2:30 – 6pm and August 16 & 29\,
  11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features **Gen Zorich
 ’s Summertime\,** highlighting the beauty of wine country and the warmth
  of long\, lazy summer days.  From Zorich’s background as a geologist a
 nd environmental scientist\, she imbues her paintings with a deep understa
 nding of the natural world. Focusing on flora\, pink waterlilies floating 
 on pastel pads in “Summer Color” engender a sense of sun-filled easy d
 ays.  These works would bring a feeling of summer contentment any time of
  year.  An award-winning artist\, Zorich has exhibited widely and has bee
 n a longtime participant in the Sonoma County Art Trails Program.\n\nMeet 
 the artist: Zorich will host the Gallery on August 2\, 11am – 2:30pm\, A
 ugust 4\, 11am to 6 pm and August 21 & 23\, 2:30 – 6pm.\n\nAlso join us 
 for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, August 6\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE
  Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event 
 celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating. This 
 month’s special theme: Music and Mocktails.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\n
 Upstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 43
 1-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** 
 \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bv
 drio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Galler
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Salsa - Tuesdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T183000
UID:260705fZzXn5oILEaNHGCkGMzMng
DESCRIPTION:Ready to dance? Join our beginner salsa class where no experie
 nce or partner is needed. Just comfortable shoes and desire to have fun!\n
 \nGreat for first timers!\n\nNo dance experience required\n\nNon-marking s
 hoes soles\n\nNo partner necessary\n\nOur relaxed environment is perfect f
 or learning salsa basics\, as we make it fun and enjoyable. In this class 
 you will learn basic directional steps\, proper frame for partner-work and
  simple turn patterns. We organize our curriculum so that the movements ar
 e easy to remember. Join us to learn the fundamentals! No experience is ne
 cessary and no partner is required. Drop-in fee is $20.\n\nDate & Time: Tu
 esdays @ 5:30PM – 6:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/beginner-salsa-tuesdays
 /17157360/2026-08-04T17
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T193000
UID:260704ZLnJmlD850GT6EoqpuZ8dw
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\nPre- requisite:\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach week\,
  we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connection 
 that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go beyond 
 the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate pat
 terns and styling\, including:\n\nTurns and Spins:\n\nMaster your inside a
 nd outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Toss moves.
 \n\nIntricate Patterns:\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, as well as va
 rious Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n\nFootwork a
 nd Styling:\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced footwork like t
 he Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work on styling with 
 a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.\n\nThis class i
 s your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead-follow connecti
 on\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your salsa vocabulary. 
 Join us and elevate your dance!\n\nDetails:\n\nNo partner necessary — ro
 tations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe so
 les to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get s
 ettled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 6:30PM – 7:30PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/intermediate-salsa-clas
 s/17159571/2026-08-04T18
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tuesdays in the Plaza: Burrows and Dilbeck (Funk/ Rock/ Soul)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T200000
UID:2606274TFuyD_N2USOoZ7T3RsqNg
DESCRIPTION:Our weekly summer concerts in the Healdsburg Plaza from 6:00 p
 .m. to 8:00 p.m. provide an eclectic and unique line-up of bands\, and hav
 e been assembled to please a wide array of musical interests. Food vendors
  will be on-hand to offer locally sourced food for sale starting at 5:00 p
 .m. with the music beginning at 6:00 p.m.\n\nAbout the band: Burrows and D
 ilbeck consists of vocalist/pianist Spencer Burrows and master guitarist /
 recording engineer Kris Dilbeck. Although they both originated from just N
 orth of San Francisco bay area ( Sonoma County )\, their musical connectio
 n hadn’t started brewing until they connected in 2002 while working on m
 usic recording projects together at Berklee College of Music in Boston\, M
 A. After their stint at Berklee concluded\, they both landed back in their
  home towns and started a group called FunKtion with musicians\, Dane Lund
 y (bass) and Aaron Haggerty (drums).\n\nFunction recorded a handful of ori
 ginal songs that were never released\, but only had one performance before
  calling it quits. The duo went on to create a new group in called Spencer
  B and the FSDs with musicians\, Emily Froberg (bass) and Cory Stück (dru
 ms) which in 2005 would be the makings of the original band\, Frobeck. In 
 just 4 years\, Frobeck would record 3 original albums\, win the Mystic The
 ater battle of the bands and be named “Best of the North Bay.” In 2010
 \, they caught the attention of management and expanded the band to includ
 e a horn section (Bari saxophonist and longtime friend\, Alex Scammon\, te
 nor saxophonist\, Alex Garcia\, and trumpeter Cayce carnahan)\, and a gros
 sly over qualified backing vocalist ( Callie Watts - who would later becom
 e Kris’ wife ).\n\nTuesdays in the Plaza is hosted by the City of Healds
 burg Community Services. At this concert we'll celebrate National Night Ou
 t\, an annual community-building campaign that promotes police-community p
 artnerships and neighborhood camaraderie.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza
URL:https://healdsburg.gov/335/Tuesdays-in-the-Plaza
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Teen & Young Adult Group
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T161500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T173000
UID:260603P2D-2Dpna0e6tBkBajfukQ
DESCRIPTION:Summer can bring a mix of freedom and uncertainty—more unstr
 uctured time\, shifting routines\, and social pressures that don’t take 
 a break. Our summer groups are designed to offer a supportive space where 
 teens and young adults can stay connected\, build skills\, and feel unders
 tood during this transition.\n\nAt Juniper & Jade Psychotherapy\, we belie
 ve growth happens in connection. These groups provide a safe\, therapist-l
 ed environment where participants can explore their experiences\, strength
 en relationships\, and build confidence in themselves.
LOCATION:Juniper & Jade Psychotherapy Inc
URL:https://juniperandjadepsychotherapy.com/group-therapy
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
