BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Painting in Fauve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260806T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260806T180000
UID:2607157y9ZeRruGUS2BFlvezPxEA
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  7/15/26\n\nAUGUST EXHIBIT: PAINT
 ING IN FAUVE\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  July 27 – August 30\, 2026\n\nRECEPTION
 : SATURDAY\, August 1\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Willow LaLand and G
 en Zorich\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be sure to t
 ake part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by
  a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.\n\nSonoma wine country a
 rtist\, Willow LaLand presents Painting in Fauve\, a collection of oil and
  acrylic paintings focusing on our region’s vibrant beauty through the a
 rtist’s Fauvist lens.  Known for her hyper-realistic landscapes\, these
  works take an imaginative turn to the fantastical\, tapping into the wild
  Fauve vivid color palette.   Highlighting the show\, “Mt. Tamalpais
 ” comes alive\, swathed in rich colors cascading over its undulating slo
 pes\, while rich foreground purple/blues heighten the mountain’s grandeu
 r.  “Fitch Mountain” similarly seems to sing with color as it overloo
 ks a lush vineyard.  LaLand’s color lens takes us from palette to palat
 e as she captures the luxuriant purple/reds of a fine red wine in “Somme
 lier’s Dream.”  Reflecting on her creative process\, LaLand notes “
 I love the artistic freedom to play\, create depth in color\, and give a t
 angible realistic impression within a completely fantastical expression.
 ”\n\nA third-generation artist\, LaLand started her studies as a young g
 irl and had a studio space at 10 years old.  She is inspired by early Ame
 rican realists and uses traditional techniques to achieve dramatic realism
 .  LaLand finds the Fauve color palette elicits a joyful response to her 
 themes of nature and wine.  Many of her collectors love both her styles a
 nd have a hard time\, though they vastly differ\, choosing between the two
 .  LaLand exhibits widely\, including internationally\, and participated 
 in the Art Trails Program.  She was featured in American Art Collector ma
 gazine in 2013 and on KRCB in 2015.\n\nMeet the artist: LaLand will host t
 he Gallery on August 2\, 2:30 – 6pm and August 16 & 29\, 11am to 6 pm.\n
 \nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Gen Zorich’s Summertime\, hi
 ghlighting the beauty of wine country and the warmth of long\, lazy summer
  days.  From Zorich’s background as a geologist and environmental scien
 tist\, she imbues her paintings with a deep understanding of the natural w
 orld. Focusing on flora\, pink waterlilies floating on pastel pads in “S
 ummer Color” engender a sense of sun-filled easy days.  These works wou
 ld bring a feeling of summer contentment any time of year.  An award-winn
 ing artist\, Zorich has exhibited widely and has been a longtime participa
 nt in the Sonoma County Art Trails Program.\n\nMeet the artist: Zorich wil
 l host the Gallery on August 2\, 11am – 2:30pm\, August 4\, 11am to 6 pm
  and August 21 & 23\, 2:30 – 6pm.\n\nAlso join us for ART NITE HEALDSBUR
 G\, Thursday\, August 6\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st
  Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and creati
 vity with over 20 galleries participating. This month’s special theme: M
 usic and Mocktails.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306
  Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 1
 1am – 6 pm.    www.upstairsart gallery.net \n\nFor further informatio
 n: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-
 1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing at Lynmar Estate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260806T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260806T143000
UID:260626EuNhQOZSV0G19Fzsv802_g
DESCRIPTION:Rooted in the bounty of Quail Hill Vineyard\, Lynmar Estate’
 s Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing invites guests to experience the flavors
  of Sonoma County at their seasonal peak. The elevated four-course menu sh
 owcases ingredients harvested from Lynmar’s organically farmed gardens\,
  orchards\, and olive groves. Each course is individually plated and thoug
 htfully paired with Lynmar’s acclaimed estate-grown Pinot Noirs\, Chardo
 nnays\, and sparkling wines\, creating a journey that is both deeply conne
 cted to Sonoma County and globally inspired. Served in the idyllic setting
  of Quail Hill Vineyard\, the experience is further enhanced by a special 
 tableside visit from Estate Chef David Frakes.\n\nCollectors Lunch Pairing
  Menu Summer 2026:\n\nAdam’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nWarm Organic 
 Popcorn\n\nWhite Corn-Kasundi Salt\, Estate Extra-Virgin Olive Oil\n\nSusa
 nna’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nThai Green Curry & Coconut Soup\n\nB
 liss Snap Peas & Heirloom Radish\n\nYoung Vines Pinot Noir\, 2021\n\nHeirl
 oom Potato & Cherry Tomato ‘Croustade’\n\nSmoked Bacon-Grain Mustard D
 ressing\n\nSusanna’s Vineyard Pinot Noir\, 2022\n\nRoasted Syrian Seven-
 Spiced Chicken Breast\n\nIndonesian Corn Fritter\, Summer Vegetable Ragout
 \, Balado Sauce\n\nRosé de Blancs Sparkling\, 2021\n\nChilled Vanilla Bur
 nt Basque Cheesecake\n\nRaspberry-Rose Syrup\, Black Tea & Licorice-Poache
 d Cherries\n\nBrown Butter Nilla Cookie\, Candied Lime\n\nEstate Ingredien
 ts:\n\nBay Laurel\, Cherries\, Chives\, Edible Flowers\, Lemons\, Olive Oi
 l\, Peas\, Potatoes\, Radishes\, Raspberries\, Thyme\, Tomatoes\, Zucchini
  and more!\n\nMenu by Estate Chef David Frakes\n\nReservations are require
 d. Maximum group size is six guests.
LOCATION:Lynmar Estate
URL:https://lynmarestate.com/reservation/type/collectors-lunch-pairing/ 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eleven Eleven: THE WE11NESS EXPERIENCE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260806T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260806T190000
UID:2606245Ptwc6p4XUqP9q1jyhBndg
DESCRIPTION:At Eleven Eleven\, wellness is more than a philosophy—it’s
  a way of life. An everyday practice rooted in being present\, savoring ea
 ch moment\, and embracing life’s simple pleasures.\n\nInspired by this b
 elief\, The We11ness Experience was created four years ago to encourage li
 ving fully and mindfully. Returning in 2026\, it invites you once again to
  engage your senses\, spark meaningful connections\, and celebrate the art
  of living well.\n\nOn the first Thursday of each month\, from April to Oc
 tober\, we’ll host guest speakers offering fresh perspectives on wellnes
 s—covering mindfulness\, emotional balance\, nutrition\, self-care\, and
  more. Each event is paired with thoughtfully curated bites and our signat
 ure Eleven Eleven wines\, all set amidst the serene beauty of our Napa Val
 ley winery.\n\nJoin us for this journey where wine and wellness come toget
 her\, creating unforgettable moments of presence\, connection\, and joy. H
 ere's to living well—uncorked and shared generously!\n\nMay: Intellectua
 l Wellness featuring Alison Levine\n\nJune: Emotional Wellness featuring M
 ayra Hernandez\n\nAugust: Occupational Wellness featuring Patrick Dossett\
 n\nSeptember: Physical Wellness featuring BodyRok & Jeannette of Poppywell
  and Swor-Yim Aesthetics\n\nOctober: Social Wellness featuring Meredith Si
 nclair\, M.Ed.\n\nFirst Thursday Of Each Month\n\nApril - June & August - 
 October 2026\n\n5:30 pm - 7:00 pm\n\nAll-Inclusive General Admission: $45 
 per person\n\nPlus\, your entry is on us when you purchase two or more bot
 tles during the event!
LOCATION:Eleven Eleven Wines
URL:https://www.elevenelevenwines.com/the-wellness-experience/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
