BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Crooked Stuff and Space Suit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T223000
UID:2607201AsPWl5vgESCRzKsxAANjA
DESCRIPTION:All ages event The Crooked Stuff and Space Suit join forces fo
 r a night of explosive sound\, blending disco-punk\, electro-funk\, post-p
 unk\, and industrial synth energy into one unforgettable live experience. 
 The Crooked Stuff brings existential discopunk for the people - a driving 
 mix of post-punk urgency\, abrasive electronics\, and danceable synth groo
 ves shaped by influences from D.C. hardcore\, Bay Area psychedelia\, funk\
 , and industrial music. Fresh off radio play across the country and perfor
 mances at Sundance Film Festival\, the trio continues building momentum ah
 ead of their upcoming album Synthetic Signals.  TheCrookedStuff.com Space 
 Suit fuses big-beat hip-hop\, funk grooves\, guitars\, and layered vocals 
 into a cosmic\, genre-bending journey inspired by unity\, expansion\, and 
 connection.  SpaceSuitMusic.com
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/the-crooked-stuff-and-space-suit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Katie Phillips\, Karen Joy Brown and Little Door @ The Lost Church
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T230000
UID:260719fLQWVaDgUkC---B4SSppPw
DESCRIPTION:Songwriters in the round with indie/folk/singer songwriters\n\
 n**Karen Joy Brown** Karen Joy Brown's elegantly sparse pop/Americana guit
 ar and deeply soulful voice disarm listeners with raw emotional honesty th
 at inspires reflection and connection. Literate lyrics reveal a poet's sou
 l with a singular sense of rhythm\, humor and compassion that leaves liste
 ners feeling uplifted and finally understood. www.karenjoybrown.com www.in
 stagram.com/karenjoybrowncreates\n\n**Katie Phillips** Singer-songwriter w
 ith a voice that stops you in your tracks and songs that stick in your rib
 cage long after the last note fades. Recognized for her extraordinary voca
 l gift since childhood\, Katie carries her father's words close: that one 
 of life's greatest honors would be using her voice as sacred offering to t
 hose she loves. Drawing from a kaleidoscope of influences\, Katie crafts v
 isceral songwriting that creates narrative universes you immediately inhab
 it. With virtuosic melodies and high craft\, she plunges you into her most
  vulnerable worries\, pains\, and tender loves\, each song startlingly int
 imate and specific. www.instagram.com/katiepsingsasong\n\n**little door** 
 begins with a simple idea: each person is a portal into deep consciousness
 \, and music is one way to open that door — or leave it ajar. Rooted in 
 psych-folk and cosmic groove\, her acoustic performances draw on themes of
  awakening\, motherhood\, love\, and the tender\, unspoken corners of the 
 psyche. Unhurried and embodied\, her live sets are the kind you feel as mu
 ch as hear — an invitation to arrive fully in yourself. www.littledoormu
 sic.com www.instagram.com/littledoor.music\n\nRecommended If You Like: *F
 iona Apple\, Annie Lennox\, Brandie Carlile\, Jenny Lewis\, CMAT\, Lana De
 l Rey\, Waxahatchee\, Mazzy Star\, Lucinda Williams*\n\n*Earlybirds!*\n\n*
 **$3 off each ticket*** *when you use the code* **earlybird5** *at check
 out. Offer ends August 2nd.*\n\n*Promo Codes are not applicable at the 
 door.*\n\n*Codes are not case sensitive\, but must be typed as one word.*
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://tinyurl.com/PhillipsJoyBrownlittledoor
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Roller Disco Daze
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T220000
UID:2607166ASK1W_MB0ydixX6dTIOsw
DESCRIPTION:Marin Center presents Roller Disco Daze\, a free community rol
 ler skating experience on Lagoon Island at the Marin County Fairgrounds. R
 unning Wednesdays through Sundays\, July 17 through August 16\, the rink i
 s open to all ages and skill levels\, with themed nights every Friday\, Sa
 turday\, and Sunday to keep things lively all summer long. \n\nSkate bene
 ath a disco ball surrounded by the lagoon\, then cool down with lawn games
 \, explore art installations by local artists on display\, and don't miss 
 the giant inflatable skate for the ultimate photo opp. A DJ spins on-site 
 beginning at 12 pm every Friday-Sunday to keep the music on point and the 
 vibes rolling. Food from Manny's Tacos will be on-site all days of the eve
 nt\, and Lobo's Ice Cream will be available July 17-19 and July 24-26.\n\n
 Admission is free. Skate rentals\, including kids' sizes\, are available o
 n-site for $5. All skaters must sign a waiver\; skaters under 18 require a
  parent or guardian signature.
LOCATION:Lagoon Island\, Marin County Fairgrounds
URL:https://marincenter.marincounty.gov/node/306
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Painting in Fauve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T180000
UID:2607153nkwNYbRa0CVRM1Sx25m1A
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  7/15/26\n\n**AUGUST EXHIBIT: PAI
 NTING IN FAUVE**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **July 27 – August 30\, 2026**\n\n*
 *RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, August 1\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Willow La
 Land and Gen Zorich\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be
  sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautif
 ul work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma wi
 ne country artist\, **Willow LaLand** presents **Painting in Fauve\,** a c
 ollection of oil and acrylic paintings focusing on our region’s vibrant 
 beauty through the artist’s Fauvist lens.  Known for her hyper-realisti
 c landscapes\, these works take an imaginative turn to the fantastical\, t
 apping into the wild Fauve vivid color palette.   Highlighting the show\
 , “Mt. Tamalpais” comes alive\, swathed in rich colors cascading over 
 its undulating slopes\, while rich foreground purple/blues heighten the mo
 untain’s grandeur.  “Fitch Mountain” similarly seems to sing with c
 olor as it overlooks a lush vineyard.  LaLand’s color lens takes us fro
 m palette to palate as she captures the luxuriant purple/reds of a fine re
 d wine in “Sommelier’s Dream.”  Reflecting on her creative process\
 , LaLand notes “I love the artistic freedom to play\, create depth in co
 lor\, and give a tangible realistic impression within a completely fantast
 ical expression.”\n\nA third-generation artist\, LaLand started her stud
 ies as a young girl and had a studio space at 10 years old.  She is inspi
 red by early American realists and uses traditional techniques to achieve 
 dramatic realism.  LaLand finds the Fauve color palette elicits a joyful 
 response to her themes of nature and wine.  Many of her collectors love b
 oth her styles and have a hard time\, though they vastly differ\, choosing
  between the two.  LaLand exhibits widely\, including internationally\, a
 nd participated in the Art Trails Program.  She was featured in American 
 Art Collector magazine in 2013 and on KRCB in 2015.\n\nMeet the artist: La
 Land will host the Gallery on August 2\, 2:30 – 6pm and August 16 & 29\,
  11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features **Gen Zorich
 ’s Summertime\,** highlighting the beauty of wine country and the warmth
  of long\, lazy summer days.  From Zorich’s background as a geologist a
 nd environmental scientist\, she imbues her paintings with a deep understa
 nding of the natural world. Focusing on flora\, pink waterlilies floating 
 on pastel pads in “Summer Color” engender a sense of sun-filled easy d
 ays.  These works would bring a feeling of summer contentment any time of
  year.  An award-winning artist\, Zorich has exhibited widely and has bee
 n a longtime participant in the Sonoma County Art Trails Program.\n\nMeet 
 the artist: Zorich will host the Gallery on August 2\, 11am – 2:30pm\, A
 ugust 4\, 11am to 6 pm and August 21 & 23\, 2:30 – 6pm.\n\nAlso join us 
 for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, August 6\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE
  Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event 
 celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating. This 
 month’s special theme: Music and Mocktails.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\n
 Upstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 43
 1-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** 
 \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bv
 drio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Galler
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Extended Run: Who Will Dance with Pancho Villa?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T193000
UID:260707kybyz0zOpEat3rosdCXgjQ
DESCRIPTION:*Who Will Dance with Pancho Villa?* played to sold-out audien
 ces in January. First performed off-Broadway in 1994\, the playwrights upd
 ated the story with the introduction of the **Ballet Folklórico Legado d
 e Mi Alegría de Cloverdale Ca** while developing the play further throug
 h the Raven Players’ ScripTease program. It is the story of a young Chic
 ano from Chicago\, lured to the East Coast by an Ivy League scholarship. A
 s he tries to make a life there\, he neglects family relationships and dee
 p cultural roots established throughout generations. It takes his mother
 ’s nearly fatal heart attack\, help from a Jewish therapist\, and the vi
 sitation of the spirits of his long dead relatives (and of his historical 
 idol\, Pancho Villa) to help him realize what he’s lost\, and how to get
  it back. Dancing spirits\, who are intertwined throughout the play\, help
  remind “Chicano” of the joy in dancing\, especially when dancing is m
 uch more than dancing.\n\nBy John and Gabriel Fraire\n\nDirected by Jenna 
 Vera Dolcini\n\n**August 7\, 8\, 9\, \\*13\, 14\, 15\, 16**\n\n**Friday an
 d Saturday Shows:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Sunday Matinee:** 2:00 PM\n\n**\\*Value 
 Thursday:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Admission: Adults:** $25\n\n**Student w/ID:** $1
 0\n\n**\\*Value Thursday Performance:** Pay What You Can
