BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Taking Parkinson's to the Mat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T213000
UID:260716sVrEt3d1ekSfzbbPB2T3Mg
DESCRIPTION:Foxflow's Fourth Annual "Taking Parkinson's to the Mat" Return
 s to Bacchus Landing August 8\n\n**Healdsburg fundraiser blends yoga\, win
 e\, live music\, and community spirit to support Parkinson's research**\n\
 nHEALDSBURG\, Calif. — July 15\, 2026 — Foxflow\, Inc.\, a Sonoma Coun
 ty nonprofit dedicated to advancing Parkinson's disease research\, will ho
 st its fourth annual "Taking Parkinson's to the Mat" fundraiser on Saturda
 y\, August 8\, 2026\, from 5 to 9 p.m. at Bacchus Landing in Healdsburg. T
 he event benefits the Michael J. Fox Foundation for Parkinson's Research (
 MJFF).\n\nThe evening kicks off with an optional\, gentle yoga flow led by
  Healdsburg instructor Shelley Gilbert\, followed by food and wine from lo
 cal vendors and Bacchus Landing's tasting rooms. Live music from Wonder Br
 ead 5 will keep guests dancing under the stars\, while an online auction a
 nd on-site raffle offer chances to win prizes throughout the night.\n\n"Ta
 king Parkinson's to the Mat" has grown into one of Sonoma County's most an
 ticipated fundraisers\, raising more than $80\,000 last year and topping $
 90\,000 this year for Parkinson's research. Funds raised support the Micha
 el J. Fox Foundation's mission to find a cure for Parkinson's disease and 
 improve treatments for those living with the condition.\n\nTickets are $65
  per person and include event entry\, the Wonder Bread 5 performance\, the
  optional yoga session\, and a Govino wine tumbler. Food\, wine\, merchand
 ise\, and additional raffle tickets are available for purchase on-site. Ti
 ckets are available now at foxflow.ejoinme.org/tickets.\n\nThe event is op
 en to guests 21 and older. Pets and emotional support animals are not perm
 itted\; service animals are welcome.\n\nSponsorship opportunities ranging 
 from $1\,000 to $10\,000+ are available for businesses and community leade
 rs who want to support Parkinson's research while connecting with an engag
 ed\, purpose-driven audience. Interested sponsors can contact Cherie Huill
 ade at cherie.huillade@colliers.com.\n\n**About Foxflow\, Inc.**\n\nFoxflo
 w is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization (EIN 99-3115074) dedicated to adva
 ncing Parkinson's disease research and supporting individuals affected by 
 the condition. Through strategic partnerships\, community involvement\, an
 d fundraising events like "Taking Parkinson's to the Mat\," Foxflow funds 
 cutting-edge research and raises awareness in support of the Michael J. Fo
 x Foundation for Parkinson's Research. Foxflow is led by President and Adm
 inistrator Benjamin Haas.\n\n**Media Contact:** Tina\, Foxflow\, Inc. tina
 @foxflow.org foxflow.org
LOCATION:Bacchus Landing
URL:http://foxflow.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
