BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Talks - Rest in Peace
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T113000
UID:260526NnCtiPwLCkqpXwNiMGFmZQ
DESCRIPTION:Death Rituals & The Cemetery’s History\n\nIn the Victorian a
 ge\, death was surrounded by strict rituals and rites. Stopped clocks\, co
 vered mirrors\, heavy black veils and jewelry woven from the deceased&\\#3
 9\;s hair were all part of the story.\n\nFran Schierenbeck will take you o
 n a tour of these rites. And Jim Dreisback will tell the history of Oak Mo
 und\, one of Sonoma County’s oldest cemeteries\, from its establishment 
 in 1859 through various owners and its renaissance in the last 10 years as
  the Museum\, local service clubs and businessmen have worked to restore t
 he old section and renovate the historic fountain.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
