DESCRIPTION:Sit & Stitch is offered the 2nd & 4th Mondays a month from 3:3
 0 to 5:30 pm. For August \, it will be the 10th & 24th. You can drop in fo
 r any amount of time. You may continue needle felting and macrame as we no
 w have all of the supplies. We also have some people learning how to knit 
 and crochet. We will also have tea\, so bring your favorite covered drink 
 container. Sit and Stitch is for people to come and work on any fiber arts
  activity that they have while visiting with others. Most people will brin
 g their own projects\, but we always have hooks\, needles\, and yarn and s
 ometimes we will offer a project with instructions that people may choose 
 to make. Let us know what you would like to learn this year. We share idea
 s\, skills\, and encouragement with each other. This summer we will be add
 ing sewing\, weaving\, and decorative mending to our regular projects of k
 nitting and crocheting. Soon\, we will also have a sewing machine availabl
 e for use. Children can come if they are accompanied one to one with an ad
 ult.
LOCATION:Guerneville Regional Library
