BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Brandlin Estate Wine & Food Tasting Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T160000
UID:260312Fn2UnhgfN0m0Ep951smmkA
DESCRIPTION:Born on the rugged slopes of Mount Veeder\, Brandlin Estate pr
 oduces wines of structure\, intensity\, and place. The Brandlin Experience
  offers an in-depth exploration of this historic vineyard site through a c
 urated tasting of five estate-grown wines—including Zinfandel from centu
 ry-old vines and the estate’s signature Cabernet Sauvignon. This seated\
 , guided experience invites guests to delve into the mountain terroir thro
 ugh the lens of small-lot winemaking. Each wine reflects the elevation\, e
 xposure\, and rocky soils that define the Brandlin Estate. For an added di
 mension\, guests may opt to include seasonal bites\, thoughtfully paired t
 o complement the structure and complexity of the wines. This experience is
  hosted at the picturesque Boathouse.
LOCATION:Brandlin Estate 
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/brandlinestate/experience/565565/the-brand
 lin-wine-food-tasting-experience?date=2026-03-12&size=2&time=10%3A00
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma River Upstream High Tide Paddle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T154500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T174500
UID:260211wtTtvjgUSUy369aJR89T0w
DESCRIPTION:When the tide is high\, the Petaluma River opens into a quiete
 r\, greener world.\n\nJoin The Floathouse crew at their central downtown d
 ock for a gentle\, guided paddle upstream\, timed to higher tides that all
 ow access beyond the downtown channel and into a tranquil tidal slough. Wi
 th extra water beneath us\, we’re able to glide into calm\, lush stretch
 es of the river that are normally out of reach.\n\nThis unhurried paddle h
 ighlights the natural beauty of the Petaluma River’s brackish\, tidal wa
 terway. Watch for great egrets\, blue herons\, snowy egrets\, turtles bask
 ing along the banks\, and abundant plant life. The calm water and peaceful
  surroundings create a deeply grounding experience—many guests say they 
 feel their stress melt away within minutes.\n\nAlong the way\, knowledgeab
 le guides share stories of the river’s ecology and human history\, offer
 ing insight into how this upper channel has shaped—and continues to shap
 e—Petaluma. It’s a rare opportunity to experience how close wild natur
 e lives to the heart of downtown.\n\nBeginner-friendly. Sit-on-top kayaks 
 and all gear provided.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/petaluma-river-upstream
 -high-tide-paddle/18032819/2026-08-15T15
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
