BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:S.R. Laws
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T000000
UID:260331I72OMltlwU-ur3QTqODDZA
DESCRIPTION:S.R. Laws: An inspiring Storyteller in Song\n\n        S.R. La
 ws is a performing and recording original musical artist whose work resona
 tes with a familiar warmth while introducing entirely fresh ideas. Hailed 
 by guitarist/promoter Scotty O’Neill as “an ORIGINAL songwriter who kn
 ows how to tell a story clearly in song\,” Laws has built a reputation f
 or songs that capture both nostalgia and innovation.\n\nEarly Influences a
 nd Musical Roots  \n\nGrowing up in Northern California\, Laws developed a
  deep bond with music at an early age. His father worked as a trash collec
 tor\, and young Scott Ray Laws \\(a.k.a. S.R. Laws\\) spent countless hour
 s digging through discarded 45-rpm records. Each discovery—whether caked
  in grime or found pristine—felt like unearthing treasure. The thrill of
  dropping the needle on something new ignited his lifelong passion for son
 g-craft.\n\nThe Texas Pilgrimage  \n\nWith only two suitcases and $500 to 
 his name\, Laws set out for Austin\, Texas—the “Live Music Capital of 
 the World.” There\, open‐mic nights and songwriter showcases became hi
 s classroom. Night after night\, he honed his craft\, forging connections 
 and absorbing the essence of Americana\, roots rock\, and modern folk.\n\n
  “It was such a treat catching your set last night—really refreshing t
 o hear something new and original. Thanks for pulling up a chair and hangi
 ng out with us—we really enjoyed the conversation and the stories behind
  your songs.” - Tripp B.\, Singer-Songwriter\n\nInfluences That Shaped H
 is Voice  \n\nLaws draws inspiration from master storytellers who paved th
 e way for heartfelt\, lyrical music. Artists who have left an indelible ma
 rk on his craft include:\n\n- John Hiatt  \n\n- Lucinda Williams  \n\n- Ro
 dney Crowell  \n\n- Neil Finn  \n\n- Patty Griffin  \n\n- Steve Earle  \n\
 n- Ron Sexsmith  \n\nTheir mastery of narrative and melody has shaped his 
 own artistic journey\, resulting in songs that feel both comfortingly fami
 liar and entirely “out there.”\n\nCritical Acclaim  \n\nColleagues and
  venue owners alike have praised his work and stage presence:  \n\n“Scot
 t Ray Laws is a unique and really cool songwriter…he digs into materials
 \, tells a story in his songs\, and has a clean baritone vocality that is 
 easy on the ears. We had a chance to meet and hang with Scott back in May
 …and I had to have him back for a Wednesday evening.” - Luigi\, Owner 
 of The Listening Room\n\n“Expect slow-burning passion and vivid music…
 the kind of energy that turns into ‘let’s stay for just one more!” -
  Doug\, Owner/Wine Maker at Spicy Vines\n\nCurrent Projects  \n\nNow based
  in Sonoma County\, California\, Laws works tirelessly as a recording\, wr
 iting & touring artist. Through over 100 gig dates a year\, intimate club 
 shows\, festival stages\, house concerts and late-night songwriter circles
 \, he invites audiences to join him on a musical journey—one heartfelt s
 tory at a time.\n\nWith a blend of classic influence\, modern vision\, and
  a voice that feels like home\, S.R. Laws continues to carve out his place
  in the American songwriting landscape.
LOCATION:Bloom Carneros
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108157636?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jumpstart Your Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T160000
UID:260629t7QA0_43vk6PUFA4l0oyMA
DESCRIPTION:Every person experiences an ebb and flow to the tides of their
  creativity. We will share space together to design\, exchange ideas\, and
  hold ourselves accountable to our unique interests! The first portion of 
 our time together will involve a check-in discussion of ‘what is'\, lead
 ing into ‘what could be'. The talk will be facilitated by Erin Partridge
 \, an art therapist with a long history of supporting people in reengaging
  with creativity. After our initial talk\, we will have some time to indiv
 idually focus on our creative practices in the space of the gallery. Befor
 e we close\, we will share anything that came up in the process. Bring you
 r ideas\, a project\, and an interest in creative community. Please be min
 dful of what you choose to show up with-something quiet\, easy to clean up
 \, and non-disruptive to your fellow creatives. Not sure where to begin? S
 ome basic materials are available\, thanks to a donation from  Blick Art M
 aterials . Open for all ages-youth under 12 with an adult chaperone please
 ! Mondays\, 1-4 PM Facilitator: Erin Partridge
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/jumpstart-your-art/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Painting in Fauve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T180000
UID:2607151bgGeGr8S0e1CaE2u7okXg
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  7/15/26\n\n**AUGUST EXHIBIT: PAI
 NTING IN FAUVE**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **July 27 – August 30\, 2026**\n\n*
 *RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, August 1\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Willow La
 Land and Gen Zorich\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be
  sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautif
 ul work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma wi
 ne country artist\, **Willow LaLand** presents **Painting in Fauve\,** a c
 ollection of oil and acrylic paintings focusing on our region’s vibrant 
 beauty through the artist’s Fauvist lens.  Known for her hyper-realisti
 c landscapes\, these works take an imaginative turn to the fantastical\, t
 apping into the wild Fauve vivid color palette.   Highlighting the show\
 , “Mt. Tamalpais” comes alive\, swathed in rich colors cascading over 
 its undulating slopes\, while rich foreground purple/blues heighten the mo
 untain’s grandeur.  “Fitch Mountain” similarly seems to sing with c
 olor as it overlooks a lush vineyard.  LaLand’s color lens takes us fro
 m palette to palate as she captures the luxuriant purple/reds of a fine re
 d wine in “Sommelier’s Dream.”  Reflecting on her creative process\
 , LaLand notes “I love the artistic freedom to play\, create depth in co
 lor\, and give a tangible realistic impression within a completely fantast
 ical expression.”\n\nA third-generation artist\, LaLand started her stud
 ies as a young girl and had a studio space at 10 years old.  She is inspi
 red by early American realists and uses traditional techniques to achieve 
 dramatic realism.  LaLand finds the Fauve color palette elicits a joyful 
 response to her themes of nature and wine.  Many of her collectors love b
 oth her styles and have a hard time\, though they vastly differ\, choosing
  between the two.  LaLand exhibits widely\, including internationally\, a
 nd participated in the Art Trails Program.  She was featured in American 
 Art Collector magazine in 2013 and on KRCB in 2015.\n\nMeet the artist: La
 Land will host the Gallery on August 2\, 2:30 – 6pm and August 16 & 29\,
  11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features **Gen Zorich
 ’s Summertime\,** highlighting the beauty of wine country and the warmth
  of long\, lazy summer days.  From Zorich’s background as a geologist a
 nd environmental scientist\, she imbues her paintings with a deep understa
 nding of the natural world. Focusing on flora\, pink waterlilies floating 
 on pastel pads in “Summer Color” engender a sense of sun-filled easy d
 ays.  These works would bring a feeling of summer contentment any time of
  year.  An award-winning artist\, Zorich has exhibited widely and has bee
 n a longtime participant in the Sonoma County Art Trails Program.\n\nMeet 
 the artist: Zorich will host the Gallery on August 2\, 11am – 2:30pm\, A
 ugust 4\, 11am to 6 pm and August 21 & 23\, 2:30 – 6pm.\n\nAlso join us 
 for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, August 6\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE
  Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event 
 celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating. This 
 month’s special theme: Music and Mocktails.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\n
 Upstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 43
 1-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** 
 \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bv
 drio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Galler
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Developing Your Drawing Eye
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T130000
UID:260627gr31dRftC0qxjUXqqD8yaA
DESCRIPTION:Mondays Weekly · 6 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nJuly 13 – August
  24\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\n
 Drawing & Painting\, Extended Classes\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\n
 Ages\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$270\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$1
 0\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$280\n\nIt’s never too late to learn to
  draw – especially when nobody’s grading you. Whether you are an abjec
 t beginner\, haven’t picked up a pencil since high school\, or you’re 
 a creative who has always felt intimidated by observational drawing\, this
  six-week class is offered with you in mind.We’ll take the mystery – a
 nd the pressure – out of drawing from observation. You’ll learn how to
  really see like an artist\, practice simple techniques step by step\, and
  build skills at your own pace. No talent required\, and perfection is off
  the table.Studying observational drawing offers a foundational skill set 
 that you will carry into every medium you might wish to explore. Discover 
 the joy of drawing and build practical skills to expand your creative expr
 ession!All materials are provided.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/developing-your-drawing-eye
 /
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
