BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Local Climate Action: Healing Land\, Healing Communities
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T130000
UID:260722A6COMImFLkywdUZoOKGCpQ
DESCRIPTION:Local Climate Action:\n\nHealing Land\, Healing Communities\n\
 nLos Cien will once again convene community leaders\, partners\, and advoc
 ates for our 5th Climate Justice program\, Local Climate Action: Healing L
 and\, Healing Communities\, on August 21\, 2026\, from 10:30 am - 1:00 pm.
 \n\nWe'll open with a blessing from Melissa Elgin\, Tribal Council Secreta
 ry of the Federated Indians of Graton Rancheria\, honoring the land on whi
 ch we gather. From there\, our panel brings together leaders doing this wo
 rk right here in Sonoma County: Dillon Williams of Hybrid Indigenous Stewa
 rdship\, Latino Service Providers\, and Aura Aguilar of North Bay Jobs Wit
 h Justice. Together they'll share what they're building and why it matters
 \, from fire resilience rooted in Traditional Ecological Knowledge\, to ta
 ckling extreme heat in neighborhoods like Roseland\, to building worker po
 wer for economic\, racial\, and climate justice. Moderator Danny Chaparro 
 of LandPaths will guide the conversation\, and we'll open the floor for au
 dience Q&amp\;A so your questions shape the discussion too. Because climat
 e work can weigh heavy\, we're also making room to breathe. Gricelda Corre
 a of On the Margins will lead a somatic practice\, offering simple tools t
 o stay grounded through climate anxiety.\n\nCome ready to learn\, ask ques
 tions\, and connect with people already doing the work\, and leave with to
 ols and community to carry it forward.\n\nProgram Format\n\n10:30 am - Net
 working &amp\; Food Trucks11:15 am - Welcome &amp\; Recognitions11:25 am -
  Blessing\n\nMelissa Elgin\, Tribal Council Secretary\, Federated Indians 
 of Graton Rancheria\n\n11:40 am - Panel\n\nModerator: Danny Chaparro\, New
  Audiences Manager\, LandPaths\n\nDillon Williams\, Owner\, Hybrid Indigen
 ous Stewardship\n\nLatino Service Providers\n\nAura Aguilar\, Lead Organiz
 er\, North Bay Jobs With Justice\n\n12:35 pm - Somatic Tools for Climate A
 nxiety\n\nGricelda Correa\, Director of Community Engagement\, On the Marg
 ins\n\n12:55 pm - Closing Call to Action
LOCATION:The Backdrop @ Becoming Independent
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/local-climate-action-heali
 ng-land-healing-communit?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
